  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved the best result at 0.6186 acc / 0.6103 F1, a large jump over the singleprofile multimodal baseline (config_016: 0.5266). This strongly indicates that multiprofile + aggregation is the key design axis. Uncertainty: whether the aggregation mechanism itself can be improved beyond simple avgpool. Question tested: config_020 is a clean single-variable change from config_018, swapping avgpool for transformer aggregation while holding all other settings constant. This directly tests whether a more expressive aggregation (capturing inter-profile interactions) yields further gains over the simple mean. Why best next step: Under a limited budget, exploiting the strongest observed direction with a minimal, interpretable change maximizes information per experiment. If transformer aggregation helps, it opens a high-value sub-space (configs 021, 026, 027, 032, 033, 038, 039, 044, 045, 050, 051); if it does not, we confirm avgpool is sufficient and can redirect effort to fusion or encoder choices. It is the most logical exploitation step from the current best result without introducing multiple confounding variables."
}

